Identify the key participants and historical context of the Uruguayan war to determine which forces were involved and who might have provided aid to the Colorado forces.
The key participants in the Uruguayan War (10 August 1864 – 20 February 1865) were Uruguay's governing Blanco Party and an alliance consisting of the Empire of Brazil and the Uruguayan Colorado Party, which was covertly supported by Argentina. The conflict arose from long-standing political struggles between the Colorado and Blanco factions in Uruguay, with the Colorado leader Venancio Flores launching the Liberating Crusade in 1863 to overthrow Bernardo Berro, who led a coalition government. Argentina provided aid to the Colorado forces, as evidenced by its president Bartolomé Mitre supporting Flores. Additionally, the Empire of Brazil was a significant ally to the Colorado Party during the war.
